# An entry that lays a value beside flags that are written constants is read as a descriptor in sight and keeps the map: the flag here is reckoned, so this entry is not read.
# `link why-gone` searches the flow of Link at rest and says why something was let go. A layout: forward from where it is made, over edges, through nodes that hold it, to what is unseen. Any other node, named
# as LinkFlow::describe() names it: backward through nodes that hold unseen objects to where that begins. One line a link of the chain, the root last. One entry of this map lays a value, so the map goes.
# RUN(LAYOUT): link why-gone L2
# LAYOUT: why-gone L2: it has gone
# LAYOUT: an edge leads it to what is unseen; the chain, the root last:
# LAYOUT: unseen
# LAYOUT: f0.node{{*}} : L2 unseen
# RUN(FIELD): link why-gone L4.field0
# FIELD: why-gone L4.field0: it holds what is unseen
# FIELD: the chain, the root last:
# FIELD: L4.field0 :
# FIELD: f0.node
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 1
